window.EN={"1":"Through what the \"mountain hermit\" Niime told them at the city of Bulgar,","2":"the truth about the \"dragons\" Bern makes use of gradually comes to light.","3":"Though troubled by what they heard, Roy and the others advance into the manor deep within Bulgar.","4":"There, former Etrurian prime minister Roartz","5":"had readied himself and lay in wait to meet Roy and the others in battle...","6":"Did you let the enemy into the manor?","7":"Argh, well, if it's come to this, there's no helping it.","8":"That brat called Roy too, I'll take him down to hell with me!","9":"Lord Roartz, word has just come from the remnants of the Djute tribe","10":"that after hiding the \"Murgleis,\" they'll rush to reinforce us.","11":"Murgleis? That weapon they call a \"Divine Weapon\"?","12":"Fine, until then, hold out no matter what it takes!","13":"So this is... the manor...","14":"It's said there's a mechanism here that lets you attack through gaps in the passage.","15":"Don't let your guard down just because you think the next space over is a wall.","16":"Do you know a lot about this building?","17":"Even looking like this, I,","18":"well, I'm known a bit for knowing things.","19":"Mind you, this bit I only just picked up in the town of Bulgar before.","20":"Niime, would you happen to know... what a \"dragon\" looks like?","21":"Oh, so you're curious after all.","22":"Yes, the other day it occurred to me,","23":"whether a \"dragon\" might also take a human form.","24":"That's so.","25":"All the \"dragons\" may well be borrowing human form right now.","26":"I don't know if it's true or false,","27":"but I've at least heard tell that there are dragonkin living alongside humans in human form.","28":"The village of Nabata...","29":"Hm? Did you say something?","30":"No, it's nothing.","31":"I don't know the details, but after the \"Scouring,\"","32":"dragons are said to have begun taking human form, or so I've seen in an old document.","33":"The \"Scouring\"...","34":"You've at least heard of it, haven't you?","35":"Yes, as a legend.","36":"\"At that time, the world's 'order' went mad,","37":"day became night, summer became winter...\" or so it's told.","38":"That's right. It's such an old thing that accounts differ depending on the text,","39":"but in any case, the \"Scouring\" was something that changed the world.","40":"What was the cause?","41":"Well now... the common account is that the \"dragons\" used great magical power,","42":"and nature's order was warped, but as for the truth, even I don't know.","43":"Still, it does seem certain that it was after this that \"dragons\" began taking human form.","44":"I can't think it's entirely unrelated.","45":"Indeed, that does seem so.","46":"Well, whatever the case, the truth about \"dragons\" lies with Bern, it seems.","47":"Hm, the manor is in disarray, just as I thought.","48":"Watch closely, you dogs of Bern.","49":"Even if I, Dayan, am left alone, I will not stop fighting.","50":"You wretches, you Etrurian curs.","51":"We'll avenge our tribe, the Djute, upon you!","52":"Are you... the general of the Etrurian army?","53":"Yes, and you are?","54":"I am one called Dayan.","55":"Dayan... sir? I feel I've heard that somewhere...","56":"First, I must give you my thanks.","57":"We have fought on and on against Bern and the tribes that became its lackeys.","58":"Before Bern's overwhelming power, we had no choice but to resist","59":"through a slow, steady fight, slipping in and watching for our chance.","60":"Thanks to your advance, the situation has turned in our favor.","61":"I see... I'm glad we could be of use.","62":"But there is one thing I wish to confirm.","63":"Once this war ends, do you intend to withdraw your troops promptly, or not?","64":"This war... you mean?","65":"That's right. The plains of Sacae belong to the people who live in Sacae.","66":"If Etruria is only going to take Bern's place here,","67":"then we will find ourselves at war with you next.","68":"Right after this war... I cannot promise that.","69":"Because we are going to advance our troops into Bern's homeland itself.","70":"What did you say... into Bern's homeland...","71":"If we only drive Bern out of Sacae here and now, the peace that follows will be only temporary.","72":"The root of this calamity must be cut out. Don't you agree?","73":"No... you're right.","74":"...I see, if that's how it is, then we too will offer our cooperation.","75":"That's much appreciated.","76":"Only, once the war with Bern is over, you must promise to withdraw your troops from Sacae.","77":"Is that acceptable?","78":"Of course. I'll gladly make that promise.","79":"Grandfather...","80":"Could it be Sue? You're safe!","81":"This army here saved me.","82":"But of those who went with me, I'm the only one who survived.","83":"I see... it must have been a fierce battle.","84":"Grandfather, please fight together with us.","85":"This army isn't the kind that would invade Sacae.","86":"...Are you certain of that?","87":"I swear it by Father Sky and Mother Earth.","88":"Understood. If you'll say that much, I'll believe it.","89":"Chieftain!","90":"Shin, is it? So you've returned. Good timing, join us and...","91":"Chieftain... I'm currently fighting as part of this army.","92":"What did you say! For the Etrurian army?","93":"Yes.","94":"......","95":"Chieftain, this army has no intention of invading Sacae.","96":"So please, Chieftain, fight alongside us too.","97":"...If it's what you say, there should be no mistake in it.","98":"Understood. Let us fight together.","99":"Grandfather...","100":"Could it be Sue? You're safe!","101":"This army here saved me.","102":"But of those who went with me, I'm the only one who survived...","103":"I see... it must have been a fierce battle.","104":"Grandfather, will you fight together with us?","105":"Yes, this army doesn't seem like the kind that would invade.","106":"I see...","107":"Chieftain!","108":"Shin, is it? So you've returned. Good timing, join us and...","109":"Chieftain... I'm currently fighting as part of this army.","110":"What did you say! For the Etrurian army?","111":"Yes.","112":"......","113":"Chieftain, this army has no intention of invading Sacae.","114":"They share the same resolve as us, to stop Bern's invasion.","115":"So please, Chieftain, fight alongside us too.","116":"...If it's what you say, there should be no mistake in it.","117":"Understood. Let us fight together.","118":"If fought against Douglas: Hmph. Talking so high and mighty, but","119":"in the end, you too serve someone stronger, don't you?","120":"From the outside, perhaps that's so.","121":"But in my heart right now, there isn't a shred of doubt.","122":"Spare me your talk!","123":"If fought against anyone else: Someone, hurry here! Will you not protect me!","124":"If I, their commander, am injured, what then!","125":"Wait, w-wait, submit to me... there's still time to turn back...","126":"The crime of raising a blade against me, I'll forgive you specially... gngh.","127":"If Sue, Shin, and Dayan are all alive, and the manor is taken within 25 turns:","128":"Next comes... Bern, at last...","129":"Lord Roy, this is terrible!","130":"It seems the survivors of the Djute tribe have barricaded themselves in some ruins nearby.","131":"Ruins?","132":"Yes, and moreover, according to a prisoner's account,","133":"a bow from the age of the Dragon-Human War is said to be kept there...","134":"You mean...! Then that would...","135":"The chance it's a \"Divine Weapon\" is high, I'd say.","136":"We can't just sit around! Let's hurry to those ruins!!","137":"If anyone of Sue, Shin, or Dayan has died, or the manor is taken on turn 26 or later:","138":"Marinus, I'd like you to send this letter to Father Yodel of Etruria.","139":"A letter, is it... might I ask what it contains?","140":"It's what I heard from Niime. About the \"dragons\" Bern makes use of.","141":"Oh! Just what sort of tale did she tell you?","142":"It would take too long to explain.","143":"I haven't sealed it yet, so it'll do if you just read over the letter.","144":"Understood. Well then, right away...","145":"...Lord Roy.","146":"Princess Guinivere, is something the matter?","147":"...From here on, it will be Bern, won't it.","148":"Yes, we are finally going to advance our army into Bern's homeland.","149":"...So, this time, could I ask you to tell me everything, to the very end?","150":"...Yes. I came here intending to do just that.","151":"...At the time, Prince Zephiel","152":"had grown up to be more than worthy as Bern's heir, hadn't he?","153":"That's what I've heard.","154":"And yet, Bern's former king came to shun Prince Zephiel?","155":"Rather... it's because my brother achieved such outstanding growth.","156":"Huh...","157":"My father, Bern's former king, was by all accounts a man of ordinary ability as a king.","158":"So my brother's outstanding talent only seemed to make our father's feelings grow colder still.","159":"......","160":"And then, one day at last, my father called my brother and said to him,","161":"\"I will bring in one fit for the position and have him marry Guinivere and take Bern's throne.\"","162":"What! ...That's too much!","163":"Even so, at the time, my brother is said to have answered that if that's how it was, so be it.","164":"But those around would not allow such a thing for my brother, who had been expected to be the next king.","165":"And so, driven to despair, my father...","166":"...Attempted to assassinate Prince Zephiel?","167":"...At a banquet, my brother was handed, by our father's own hand, a cup laced with poison.","168":"And that was, for my brother, the first and last cup he ever received from our father...","169":"After returning to his room, my brother began to suffer,","170":"and for more than ten days after that, he hovered between life and death.","171":"Sheltered by General Murdock, who had raised him,","172":"my brother somehow managed to survive.","173":"...And after that, did the king do nothing more?","174":"...No.","175":"He came to regard General Murdock, who had saved my brother, and my brother's mother too as obstacles,","176":"and is said to have schemed to do away with my brother along with them.","177":"My brother, still confined to a sickbed, learned of this and feigned his own death...","178":"and when our father came to confirm my brother's death, from within the coffin... with a sword...","179":"......","180":"At the time, I was still young, and could never have understood such circumstances.","181":"All I understood was that, from that day on, the day our father died, the smile vanished from my brother's face.","182":"Until then, he could be strict, but he was a warm, gentle brother. That's why...","183":"Princess Guinivere...","184":"That's why, deep in my heart, I believe my brother hasn't changed.","185":"Someday, surely, he will return to being that kind Zephiel, my brother.","186":"Believing that... I've gone on believing that, all this time...","187":"So that's how it was...","188":"...But now, my brother is somewhere my voice can no longer reach.","189":"Lord Roy, I beg you. Please... please stop my brother.","190":"Please make him stop tormenting the people of Bern and other lands any further.","191":"Even if it means I must appeal to him by the sword?","192":"...From the moment I entrusted everything to you, Lord Roy, I made up my mind.","193":"Understood. I will surely stop King Zephiel!","194":"I swear it upon the \"Fire Emblem\" entrusted to me by the Princess!"};
